  "final_message": "Done. The app is built on the scaffold with no Dockerfile or dependency-lock changes needed (stdlib expat + Werkzeug hashing on the backend).\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201, 409 on duplicate), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 `{\"token\"}`), Bearer tokens stored in SQLite under `./data/app.db`; protected routes answer 401.\n- `POST /api/validate/xml` returns `valid`, `error`, `line`, `column`, `root_element`; `POST /api/validations` saves the same plus `xml_preview` (first 200 chars); `GET /api/validations` (`valid`/`page`/`page_size`, newest first, `{\"items\", \"total\", \"page\", \"page_size\"}`); `DELETE /api/validations/{id}` \u2014 all scoped to the owner only.\n- Well-formedness via `xml.parsers.expat`: first error position (1-based line/column), root element even for broken docs, DTD processing off and external entity refs fail closed \u2014 nothing outside the submitted text is ever fetched.\n\n**Frontend** (React + TS + Vite, Tailwind v4 via PostCSS, one entry CSS file):\n- Register/sign-in forms; signed-in username + sign-out.\n- Textarea with file loading and a Check button; green \"Well-formed\" badge with root element, or error + `line, column` with the offending line (and a column caret) highlighted in a rendered document view.\n- For signed-in users: a Save toggle, saved-check history with All/Valid/Invalid filter, delete buttons, and paging.\n\nVerified: 47 API assertions via Flask test client, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm ci && npm run build` reproducible, and a live gunicorn run covering health, static/SPA serving, auth, XXE safety, cross-user isolation, and data persistence across restart.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
  "max_turns_hit": false,
